# Test: OSPF multi-area LFA suppression (RFC 5286 Section 6.3).
#
# VALIDATES: spec-ospf-ext-6 -- intra-area prefixes always get a backup;
# inter-area routes with more than one alternate ABR, external routes with more
# than one ASBR, and backbone inter-area/external routes with virtual links are
# suppressed (left unprotected) to avoid a micro-loop where the real path leaves
# the area.
# PREVENTS: an inter-area/external LFA micro-looping in a leakage topology.
#
# Live multi-area FRR failover is owned by the ospf-lfa-frr interop scenario.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=go test -v ./internal/plugins/ospf/spf -run 'Test(LFASuppressedMultiAreaLeakage|LFAEligibilityByRouteType)$' -count=1:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=TestLFASuppressedMultiAreaLeakage
expect=stdout:contains=TestLFAEligibilityByRouteType
